    "created_at": "2018-03-07T01:40:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-07T01:41:24Z",
    "body": "Screen readers already associate labels via the for=\"\" attribute or label wrapping.\r\n\r\nAnd yes, as you noted, div was the perfect container for dt/dd groups as well. It's the same thing.\r\n\r\nScreen readers are fortunately not restricted to never look inside or outside of an element. That would make them pretty useless.\r\n\r\nThere are CSS selectors proposed for selecting the label of an input, in the case when you are unable or unwilling to use the for=\"\" attribute or a wrapper div or the sibling combinator. Because there are so many alternatives, this has been a pretty low priority for the CSS working group.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
