    "created_at": "2018-03-07T01:57:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-07T01:57:37Z",
    "body": "> And yes, as you noted, div was the perfect container for dt/dd groups as well. It's the same thing.\r\n\r\nI didn't understand the rational back then, and I don't understand it now. I can't see how div is the perfect semantic choice...\r\n\r\nHaving a polymorphic container that only has meaning after parsing its outer AND/OR inner context is hard to program, hard to understand by human users and error prone while copying/past/cutting parts of html documents.\r\n\r\nI value the explicit containers we got. They are easy to read, understand, maintain as programmers as well as as users. They are easy to work with when manipulating html documents.\r\n\r\nAre there any (open) proposals you can think of that feature semantic containers/wrappers where you think they are worth it?\r\n\r\nIf having a polymorphic container would be enough, why not just use div+header within form instead of fieldset+legend?\r\n\r\n* * *\r\n\r\nSelecting the label by going through the input in terms of css selectors would be a great thing because it will reduce clutter/div/class-soup. Do you have a ticket in mind where I can read about the current state of the proposal?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
